+Go file by file, line by line. For each file provide:
+
+1. PURPOSE — what this file does and its role in the system
+2. IMPORTS & DEPENDENCIES — every library used and why
+3. FUNCTIONS & CLASSES — explain each one in detail
+4. LINE BY LINE LOGIC — walk through the core logic step by step
+5. BUGS & ERRORS — any broken, deprecated, or problematic code
+6. PERFORMANCE ISSUES — bottlenecks, inefficiencies, redundant code
+7. SECURITY ISSUES — any vulnerabilities or unsafe practices
+8. DEAD CODE — unused variables, functions, imports
+9. IMPROVEMENT SUGGESTIONS — specific fixes with code examples
+
+After analyzing all files:
+10. ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW — how all files connect together
+11. DATA FLOW — how data moves from webcam → gaze detection → mouse control
+12. CRITICAL BUGS — the most urgent things to fix first
+13. PRIORITY ACTION LIST — ordered list of what to fix/improve
+
+This is a Python eye tracking project using:
+- MediaPipe for facial landmark detection
+- OpenCV for webcam feed processing
+- Polynomial regression for gaze-to-screen calibration
+- Mouse control for hands-free accessibility
+- WebSocket or socket server for communication
+
+Be thorough. Do not skip any file or any function.

